      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! For WCAG 2.1 compliance on color contrast ratios, first check that all text has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text. Use online tools like WebAIM's Color Contrast Checker for quick analysis. For screen reader compatibility, ensure all functionality is navigable via keyboard, simplified and logical code structures are used, and provide proper ARIA labels for icons and buttons. Conduct manual testing with popular mobile screen readers like VoiceOver. I recommend also consulting the Mobile Accessibility Quick Reference Guide from the W3C.",
