      "content": "Unpredictable bugs are indeed challenging, but they can be framed as opportunities for robustness in your demonstration. First, acknowledge that all software has non-deterministic elements, known as edge cases, which can manifest due to the complex interactions within the app or inconsistencies in operating environments. Emphasize that finding and fixing these irregularities is part of a validation process that aims to improve software quality. Describe your approach to these issues as a 'path to improvement,' highlighting the thorough testing cycles that aim to catch these elusive bugs. By presenting them as part of a commitment to continual refinement, stakeholders can appreciate the process as a strength, signaling proactive dedication to excellence, rather than a lapse in reliability.",
      "source": "target",
